<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malaysian Indian Congress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1946">1946</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Malayan Indian Congress, MIC</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Malaysian Indian Congress, founded in 1946 as the Malayan Indian Congress, is a political party representing the Indian community of Malaysia, many of them descended from plantation labourers brought in under British rule. It joined the Alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-malays-national-organisation">United Malays National Organisation</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaysian-chinese-association">Malayan Chinese Association</a> in 1954, sharing in the victory of 1955 and in independence in 1957, and remained a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malaysian-indian-congress.jpg" alt="Malaysian Indian Congress" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Malaysian Indian Congress, redraw by Molecule Extraction · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malaysian_Indian_Congress_Logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
